@startuml

salt
{
  <b>ORE STUDIO - SYSTEM ADMINISTRATION: OPERATIONS</b>
  --
  <b>HOUSEKEEPING</b>  |  Stores (9) | Runs (8)
  --
  {
    Stores: 9 | Policies: 7 | <color:#b00020>Unbounded: 1</color> | Measured: 2.5 GB across 7 stores
  }
  --
  <b><color:#b00020>1 of the 9 stores is unbounded.</color></b>
  The catalogue declares a default bound for every store that can take one, and 7
  policies hold here, so every other store is bounded by a policy or by its content
  digest. An unbounded store is never deleted from: it grows until the database or
  the disk is full. The calendar dates are the gap: a policy bounds by age, and a
  day behind the horizon is out of range rather than old.
  [ Show the 1 unbounded ]   [ Open the runs log ]
  --
  <b>EVERY STORE</b>                                  [ Unbounded (1) ]   7 policies · 9 stores
  A store with no policy that applies is kept for ever.
  {#
    Store (shape) | Bounded? | Bounded by | Size | Growth
    Calendar dates (chunked) | <color:#b00020>Unbounded</color> | none -- no policy | 283 MB | +652 kB/wk
    Report run cashflows (chunked) | Bounded | drop chunks, 90 days | 186 MB of 512 MB | +16.9 MB/wk
    Report run metrics (chunked) | Bounded | drop chunks, 90 days | 4 MB | +372 kB/wk
    Market data delivery counts (ordinary) | Bounded | delete rows, 30 days | 29 MB | +2.5 MB/wk
    Market data ticks (chunked) | Bounded | drop chunks, 90 days | 16 kB | flat
    Compute job inputs (prefix) | Bounded | expire objects, 7 days | not measured | not measured
    Compute job outputs (prefix) | Bounded | expire objects, 90 days | not measured | not measured
    Compute node scratch (host directory) | Bounded | release directory, 1 day | 1.9 GB of 2.0 GB | +145.7 MB/wk
    Engine package cache (package cache) | Bounded by keying | content digest | 209 MB | +19 MB/wk
  }
  --
  Each row also states the cost of having no bound: about 33 MB a year for the
  calendars, about 7.4 GB a year for the node scratch, at the rate of the last
  twelve weeks. A row opens that store's own page, where the plot, the policy and
  the activity are. The plot is not in the list. Unbounded is red because there is
  no reading of it that is not bad.
}

@enduml
